  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of lutetium (177Lu) oxodotreotide: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.V_Various.V10X_OtherTherapeuticRadiopharmaceuticals.V10XX04_Lutetium177luOxodotreoti.Lutetium177luOxodotreotide_Sood2026_netter_1_estimate\">Lutetium177luOxodotreotide_Sood2026_netter_1_estimate</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of lutetium (177Lu) oxodotreotide in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Lutetium177luOxodotreotide_Barakat2023_base</code></li><li><code>Lutetium177luOxodotreotide_Barakat2023_final</code></li><li><code>Lutetium177luOxodotreotide_Sood2026_netter_1_estimate</code></li><li><code>Lutetium177luOxodotreotide_Sood2026_netter_p_estimate</code></li></ul><h4>About lutetium (177Lu) oxodotreotide</h4><p>Lutetium (177Lu) oxodotreotide is a therapeutic radiopharmaceutical used to treat neuroendocrine tumours. It is authorised in the European Union, where it is used in specialised settings for this indication.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q27273888\">Wikidata Q27273888</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Lutetium177LuOxodotreotide\">Lutetium177LuOxodotreotide</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>10/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 86400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
